# 0008 xg: give the compositor's frames GGTT slots so the plane can scan them out directly
#
# Base:  NvGfx xe 5a19a73f36249efb99c44c3f9cb34603ef0c0eb8 (XeGfx 0.0.44)
# Requires: patches/0001-xg_vm-userptr-race.patch (touches the same tree, not these files)
# Files: gpu/xegfx/shim/include/xg_i915.h (modified)
#        gpu/xegfx/shim/src/xnu/xg_kext.cpp (modified)
#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/xg_i915_exec.c (modified: expose xg_i915_dev() and xg_i915_idle())
#        gpu/xkpi/src/i915/xg_i915_flip.c (new)
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0008-core-ggtt-flip-slots.patch
#
# The accelerator owns the display pipe but the frame the compositor hands it lives in system memory.
# This side already owns the GGTT page tables, so it reserves a few slots in the global GGTT
# (i915_gem_gtt_insert with I915_COLOR_UNEVICTABLE), rewrites a slot's PTEs for a frame's physical pages
# (ggtt->vm.insert_page + ggtt->invalidate) and exposes three kernel calls through the XeGfxResident
# callPlatformFunction bridge: xgFlipInit / xgFlipMap / xgFlipUnmap.  xg_i915_dev() lets the other file reach
# the i915_private that the driver-side KPI already looked up.  Slots are never freed; unmapping just points
# the slot at a scratch page so nothing stale can be scanned out.
# Later phase (K9): the flip is armed by the accelerator's deferred worker instead of synchronously, so the
# core side also exposes the idle probe xg_i915_idle() through the same bridge ("xgFlipQuery"): 1 when every
# engine finished the requests it was given, 0 while busy, -ENODEV without an i915 device.  It does not sleep.
#

